.TH AD_SESSION 1 "2026-09-03" "ad 2.0" "ad tools"
.SH NAME
ad_session \- vim-only interactive op debugger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_session
<oldfile> <newfile> [opfile] [options]
.br
.B ad_session
--resume <session_dir>
.br
.B ad_session
--resume-latest
.br
.B ad_session
--list-sessions
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_session
creates a session directory under
.I ad_sessions/
in the project root, copies old/new files, generates ops, initializes a
git repo, and launches vim with a split layout:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Left split: diff (new vs result) \(em updated on F6
.IP \(bu 2
Right top: ops.tsv (editing, F5=animate, F6=snapshot)
.IP \(bu 2
Right bottom: result.txt (updated on F6)
.RE
.PP
No tmux required. Everything runs inside vim.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BI --ad-layer= NAME
Layer(s) for ad_gen_ops (if generating ops). Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --session-name= NAME
Custom session directory name.
.TP
.BI --resume= PATH
Resume existing session.
.TP
.B --resume-latest
Resume most recent session.
.TP
.B --list-sessions
List sessions and exit.
.TP
.B --no-generate
Don't generate ops if opfile missing.
.TP
.BI --fold-context= N
Context lines around non-keep ops (default: 5).
.TP
.B --fold-hunks
Start with all hunks folded.
.SH VIM SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F5
Run animation in terminal split.
.TP
.B F6
Run animator (snapshot), update result.txt, refresh diff.
.TP
.B <leader>r
Same as F6.
.TP
.B <leader>c
Git commit in session dir.
.TP
.B <leader>q
Commit and quit.
.TP
.B <leader>Q
Quit without committing.
.TP
.B <leader>g
Regenerate ops (backs up to ops.tsv.bak).
.TP
.B <leader>d
Reopen diff split (result vs new).
.TP
.B <leader>h
Fold all hunks except current.
.TP
.B <leader>H
Unfold all hunks.
.TP
.B <leader>k
Toggle keep-op folding.
.TP
.B <leader>?
Show help (shortcuts).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
New session with generated ops:
.B ad_session old.py new.py --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder
.TP
Custom session name:
.B ad_session old.py new.py --session-name bug42
.TP
Resume latest:
.B ad_session --resume-latest
.TP
List sessions:
.B ad_session --list-sessions
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_tmux_watch (1),
.BR ad_watch (1),
.BR ad_gen_ops (1),
.BR ad (1)
